eturn9view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn2view2\",\"lineno\":70}); Total lines: 165\nL0: 【0†iframe】【1†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2: ## Files\nL3: #\nL4: \nL5: p3_sumcheck/zk/\nL6: mod.rs\nL7: \nL8:     `【2†1】//! Honest-verifier zero-knowledge sumcheck for WHIR.\nL9:     【3†2】//!\nL10:     【4†3】//! Implements Construction 6.3 of eprint 2026/391 on top of both\nL11:     【5†4】//! stacked-binding modes — prefix and suffix.\nL12:     【6†5】//!\nL13:     【7†6】//! # Overview\nL14:     【8†7】//!\nL15:     【9†8】//! The plain WHIR sumcheck leaks the witness:\nL16:     【10†9】//! Each round polynomial coefficient is an affine function of the secret message.\nL17:     【11†10】//!\nL18:     【12†11】//! The HVZK variant blinds those coefficients with `k` small mask polynomials, one per sumcheck round.\nL19:     【13†12】//! Overhead: only `O(k * ell_zk)` extra field elements.\nL20:     【14†13】//!\nL21:     【15†14】//! # Protocol shape\nL22:     【16†15】//!\nL23:     【17†16】//! Let `k` be the folding factor and `ell_zk` the mask code message length.\nL24:     【18†17】//!\nL25:     【19†18】//! 1. Prover samples `k` univariate masks of degree `ell_zk - 1` over the extension field.\nL26:     【20†19】//! 2. The masks are batch encoded under a zero-knowledge code, MMCS-committed\nL27:     【21†20】//!    as one matrix, and absorbed into the Fiat-Shamir transcript.\nL28:     【22†21】//! 3. Prover sends `mu_tilde`, the sum of all mask evaluations over `{0,1}^k`.\nL29:     【23†22】//! 4. Verifier samples a combining challenge `eps` in the extension field.\nL30:     【24†23】//! 5. Per-round wire polynomial mixes:\nL31:     【25†24】//!    - the live mask,\nL32:     【26†25】//!    - past mask evaluations at sampled challenges,\nL33:     【27†26】//!    - future-mask endpoints,\nL34:     【28†27】//!    - the plain sumcheck contribution scaled by `eps`.\nL35:     【29†28】//!\nL36:     【30†29】//! # Round polynomial at a glance\nL37:     【31†30】//!\nL38:     【32†31】//! For round `j` with past challenges `gamma_1, ..., gamma_{j - 1}`:\nL39:     【33†32】//!\nL40:     【34†33】//! ```text\nL41:     【35†34】//!     h_j(X) = 2^{k - j}     * s_j(X)\nL42:     【36†35】//!            + 2^{k - j}     * sum_{l <  j} s_l(gamma_l)\nL43:     【37†36】//!            + 2^{k - j - 1} * sum_{l >  j} ( s_l(0) + s_l(1) )\nL44:     【38†37】//!            + eps           * plain_piece_j(X)\nL45:     【39†38】//! ```\nL46:     【40†39】//!\nL47:     【41†40】//! Verifier checks:\nL48:     【42†41】//!\nL49:     【43†42】//! ```text\nL50:     【44†43】//!     round 1  : h_1(0) + h_1(1) = eps * mu + mu_tilde\nL51:     【45†44】//!     round j>1: h_j(0) + h_j(1) = h_{j - 1}(gamma_{j - 1})\nL52:     【46†45】//! ```\nL53:     【47†46】//!\nL54:     【48†47】//! # Module layout\nL55:     【49†48】//!\nL56:     【50†49】//! - Proof record and mask oracle handle.\nL57:     【51†50】//! - Fiat-Shamir description of one masked batch, driven by every party.\nL58:     【52†51】//! - Prover-side sumcheck with mask sampling and round-polynomial assembly.\nL59:     【53†52】//! - Verifier-side replay with the dropped-coefficient reconstruction.\nL60:     【54†53】//! - Witness-free simulators, one per prelude, used to prove honest-verifier zero-knowledge.\nL61:     【55†54】//!\nL62:     【56†55】//! # Two preludes, and the scope of each\nL63:     【57†56】//!\nL64:     【58†57】//! A masked batch reaches its target one of two ways, and the description names which:\nL65:     【59†58】//!\nL66:     【60†59】//! ```text\nL67:     【61†60】//!     recorded claims  ->  the target is derived from the claims a verifier recorded\nL68:     【62†61】//!     inherited claim  ->  the target arrives as public input and is bound first\nL69:     【63†62】//! ```\nL70:     【64†63】//!\nL71:     【65†64】//! The composed WHIR pipeline plays the inherited one, at every batch, on both sides.\nL72:     【66†65】//!\nL73:     【67†66】//! The recorded-claims prelude is this crate's own standalone surface instead.\nL74:     【68†67】//! No in-tree pipeline plays it: its entry points serve callers who drive a masked batch directly, and it stays supported on that basis.\nL75:     【69†68】//!\nL76:     【70†69】//! Both preludes carry a witness-free simulator, so neither ships without its zero-knowledge argument.\nL77:     【71†70】//!\nL78:     【72†71】//! Scope, so a future reader can act on it: a third prelude owes a third simulator.\nL79:     【73†72】//! Retiring the recorded-claims prelude means retiring the public entry points that expose it, which is an API decision rather than a change inside this module.\nL80:     【74†73】//!\nL81:     【75†74】//! # Layout coverage\nL82:     【76†75】//!\nL83:     【77†76】//! Both stacked-binding modes are supported.\nL84:     【78†77】//! The masking layer is binding-agnostic; only the residual handoff differs between modes.\nL85:     【79†78】//! Resolves [Plonky3#1649](https://github.com/Plonky3/Plonky3/issues/1649).\nL86:     【80†79】//!\nL87:     【81†80】//! # Field constraints (Lemma 6.4)\nL88:     【82†81】//!\nL89:     【83†82】//! - Base field characteristic must not be `2`.\nL90:     【84†83】//! - Mask message length `ell_zk` must be at least `3`, so the mask (degree `ell_zk - 1`) covers the degree-2 plain round polynomial.\nL91:     【85†84】//!\nL92:     【86†85】//! Both are checked where the transcript description is built.\nL93:     【87†86】//!\nL94:     【88†87】//! A prover treats a violation as its own configuration bug.\nL95:     【89†88】//!\nL96:     【90†89】//! A verifier reports it.\nL97:     【91†90】//!\nL98:     【92†91】//! # Divergences from the paper\nL99:     【93†92】//!\nL100:     【94†93】//! ## `ell_zk >= 3`, against the paper's `ell_zk >= 2`\nL101:     【95†94】//!\nL102:     【96†95】//! The round polynomial here is a product of two multilinears, so it is quadratic in `X`.\nL103:     【97†96】//!\nL104:     【98†97】//! ```text\nL105:     【99†98】//!     h_size = max(ell_zk, 3)\nL106:     【100†99】//!\nL107:     【101†100】//!     ell_zk = 2  ->  mask covers slots 0, 1 only, and slot 2 carries eps * c_inf alone\nL108:     【102†101】//!     ell_zk = 3  ->  mask covers slot 2 as well\nL109:     【103†102】//! ```\nL110:     【104†103】//!\nL111:     【105†104】//! At `ell_zk = 2` the quadratic coefficient would ship unmasked, so the bound is deliberately one higher.\nL112:     【106†105】//!\nL113:     【107†106】//! ## The `aux * 2^{-j}` carry\nL114:     【108†107】//!\nL115:     【109†108】//! An inherited batch adds an auxiliary constant to its target, matching Definition 5.8.\nL116:     【110†109】//!\nL117:     【111†110】//! The carry is the normalisation that makes it behave like a constant function on the cube.\nL118:     【112†111】//!\nL119:     【113†112】//! ```text\nL120:     【114†113】//!     AUX * 2^{-k} at every point of {0,1}^k\nL121:     【115†114】//!\nL122:     【116†115】//!     round-j partial sum  ->  2^{k-j} * AUX * 2^{-k}  =  AUX * 2^{-j}\nL123:     【117†116】//!     cube total           ->  2^{k}   * AUX * 2^{-k}  =  AUX\nL124:     【118†117】//! ```\nL125:     【119†118】//!\nL126:     【120†119】//! Round `j` therefore adds `eps * AUX * 2^{-j}` to its constant slot, and the residual carries `eps * AUX * 2^{-k}`.\nL127:     【121†120】//!\nL128:     【122†121】//! ## Compiled hiding is computational, not perfect\nL129:     【123†122】//!\nL130:     【124†123】//! Lemma 6.4 is proved for an IOR whose masks are oracles, with a simulator answering queried positions.\nL131:     【125†124】//!\nL132:     【126†125】//! ```text\nL133:     【127†126】//!     paper     ->  mask oracle, only the queried positions are ever seen\nL134:     【128†127】//!     this code ->  the whole mask codeword committed under one MMCS root\nL135:     【129†128】//! ```\nL136:     【130†129】//!\nL137:     【131†130】//! A root determines the masks information-theoretically, so indistinguishability of the commits rests on the commitment hiding a high-entropy leaf set.\nL138:     【132†131】//!\nL139:     【133†132】//! Perfect indistinguishability still holds for everything the simulator itself